   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-01-16">16th January 1942</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor Paul Tillich</rs><lb/>
               Union Theological Seminary<lb/>
               Broadway and 120th St.<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I read with great deal of interest your three articles on war aims which the <hi
                  rend="underline">Protestant</hi> reprinted. I hope that they are very widely
               read.</p>
            <p>I think that you will certainly be interested in <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4218"
                  type="person">Percy Corbett</rs>&apos;s book POST-WAR WORLDS, which we are
               publishing on January 29th. Much of his thinking runs very close to yours. <rs
                  ref="#" type="person"
                  >Reinie<!-- unklar, wer gemeint ist, wahrscheinlich Reinhold Niebuhr? tillich_person_id__1390 --></rs>
               has a copy and thinks very highly of the book.</p>
            <p>With all good wishes,</p><closer>
               <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3458" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">J. King Gordon</hi> J. King Gordon</rs></signed><lb/>
               JKG:hh
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
